cat > /fs04/ar57/wenyu/GeneRec/results/research/issue117/runs/run_2b579f1172754102/agents/review/review.json <<'EOF'
{
  "candidate_id": "geometry-directed-residual-poincare-v1",
  "candidate_sha256": "b537eaa57417a3bf9ec048e75ecbecd74a92ccc938eafda05d5affcaa89caa22",
  "verdict": "MATERIAL",
  "blockers": [
    {
      "severity": "MATERIAL",
      "issue": "The registered comparisons are not mechanically reproducible from this manifest because the frozen paired seed set and the exact referenced admission-reference/Stage3 protocol are not specified here.",
      "evidence": "protocol.training_protocol refers to the 'exact frozen admission-reference ... seeds' without identifying that reference or enumerating seeds, epochs, batch size/order, optimizer schedule, and KMeans initialization. falsifier.stage3_behavioral_test.seed_rule likewise says 'paired frozen seeds' and 'frozen downstream T5 Stage3 protocol' without defining either. The test is properly registered as test_R@10, curved-minus-flat > 0, minimum effect 0.005, arithmetic mean paired difference, once per arm/seed, with no test-based fitting/selection/threshold adjustment; however, an independent evaluator cannot determine the registered seed combination or reproduce the frozen protocol from this candidate manifest alone."
    }
  ],
  "reproducible_evidence": {
    "schema_and_identity": "schema_version is 1, matching the frozen schema version. candidate_id and candidate_sha256 are copied from the current-only manifest.",
    "causal_link_design_claim": "The train-only transition population and stated no-reverse fraction motivate a directional next-item problem, but do not establish negative curvature or causal improvement. The learned shared map A is applied only to the source representation in the directed successor loss, so the source/target scoring roles differ. The candidate appropriately frames negative curvature as a hypothesis and registers a flat matched control and downstream behavioral falsification rather than claiming the observed asymmetry proves hyperbolic necessity.",
    "math_and_numerics": "The stated Poincare squared distance is well-typed for 32-vectors and, for c=0.5 and projected norms at most R=0.9, denominators are positive because cR^2=0.405<1. The acosh argument is at least 1; the declared stable expression log1p(u+sqrt(u*(u+2))) is the acosh(1+u) identity for u>=0. The c->0 squared-distance limit 4*||x-y||^2 is correct, and the stated unsquared limit is 2*||x-y||. The flat arm explicitly bypasses the singular curved projection radius and retains the common fixed projection. No undefined numerical domain or non-flat-limit defect is apparent in the specified distance.",
    "loss_and_targets": "L_q has compatible [N,256] assignment weights and vector-valued projected distance operands; its epoch-frozen Q is explicitly stop-gradient. L_tr has a fixed train-item candidate universe, includes the observed successor, excludes the source, retains transition multiplicity, and defines a source-only learned map. The target and candidate set are train-only and parameter-independent. The combined objective and empty/invalid handling are stated sufficiently to determine its targets and reductions.",
    "same_capacity_control": "The control specifies one implementation, identical architecture and parameter count, inputs, train-only transition signal, fixed projection, assignment procedure, initialization and optimizer/protocol, with the sole scored-distance substitution being D_c^2 versus its c->0 limit. This is an appropriate same-capacity metric control as designed; it is not a GPU-approval finding.",
    "leakage_and_stage2_role": "The manifest prohibits validation/test behavior and prediction-time user context from Stage2 optimization; validation pairs are read-only diagnostics, train transitions are the only behavioral Stage2 targets, and test is reserved for one downstream Stage3 evaluation without fitting or selection. Stage2 emits global item SIDs and does not rank. The registered leading diagnostics include validation Hard-L1 ER, distinct ordered two-token prefixes, and L3/conditional-G3 statistics; the behavioral question is separately registered downstream as test_R@10.",
    "thresholds_and_classification": "Admission gates name valid_l1_hard_er and level2_distinct_prefixes and refer to the frozen strict thresholds (>10.0 and >16145); the comparative falsifier separately gives positive directions and minimum effects for those metrics and conditional_G3. The Stage3 test registers direction and a 0.005 minimum effect. Pass/falsified/mixed classifications explicitly account for NULL seeds, missing/undefined evaluations, and empty strata. The classification rules are intelligible, but their seed/protocol inputs are not recoverable as noted in the blocker."
  }
}
EOF

